"facts": [
{"group":"GenAI and vets details","items":[
 {"text":"genai-service answers vet questions from an in-memory vector store pre-embedded in <code>vectorstore.json</code>; the live call to vets-service happens only if that file is missing.",
  "evidence":[
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/genai/VectorStoreController.java:58","quote":"load(resource)"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/genai/AIDataProvider.java:66","quote":"this.vectorStore.similaritySearch(sr)"}]},
 {"text":"Chat memory keeps context across messages (a <code>MessageChatMemoryAdvisor</code> is registered on the chat client).",
  "evidence":[{"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/genai/PetclinicChatClient.java:48","quote":"MessageChatMemoryAdvisor.builder(chatMemory)"}]},
 {"text":"vets-service caches <code>GET /vets</code> in a cache named <code>vets</code>; caching is switched on only under the <code>production</code> profile. The config repo sets <code>vets.cache.ttl: 60</code> and <code>heap-size: 100</code>, bound to <code>VetsProperties</code>.",
  "evidence":[
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-vets-service/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vets/system/CacheConfig.java:28","quote":"@Profile(\"production\")"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-vets-service/src/main/resources/application.yml:7","quote":"cache-names: vets"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices-config:vets-service.yml:3","quote":"ttl: 60"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-vets-service/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vets/system/VetsProperties.java:25","quote":"@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = \"vets\")"}]},
 {"text":"Caffeine is on the vets-service classpath as the cache library.",
  "evidence":[{"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-vets-service/pom.xml:81","quote":"<artifactId>caffeine</artifactId>"}]},
 {"text":"In the docker profile vets-service listens on 8083 and genai-service on 8084; otherwise the shared config gives services a random port.",
  "evidence":[
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices-config:vets-service.yml:22","quote":"port: 8083"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices-config:genai-service.yml:16","quote":"port: 8084"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:4","quote":"# start services on random port by default"}]},
 {"text":"The LLM key is read from the environment (<code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>) and docker-compose forwards it to genai-service.",
  "evidence":[
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:85","quote":"OPENAI_API_KEY=${OPENAI_API_KEY}"}]},
 {"text":"genai-service also pulls in the Spring Cloud Gateway starter and JPA/HSQLDB in its pom, although no gateway routes or entities were found in its source.",
  "evidence":[
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/pom.xml:80","quote":"spring-cloud-starter-gateway-server-webflux"},
   {"ref":"spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/pom.xml:53","quote":"spring-boot-starter-data-jpa"}]}
]}
]
